const body = `<h1>6.5b — FixedInventory.java: Array-Based Backpack</h1>

<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">RPG Build</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        You have Item objects. Now you need somewhere to put them. You'll build
        <code>FixedInventory.java</code> — a container that holds items in a plain
        array, tracks how many slots are used, and handles add/remove/search operations.
        This is the array-based collection pattern you'll see everywhere in CS.
    </p>

    <p>
        Open the <a href="../docs/unit-06/inventory-builder.html">Inventory Builder
        (Student RPG Guide)</a> File 2: FixedInventory.java.
    </p>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Build: FixedInventory.java</h3>
        <p>Create <code>FixedInventory.java</code>:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Private fields: <code>Item[] items</code> and <code>int count</code></li>
            <li>Constructor takes capacity, creates the array</li>
            <li><code>add(Item item)</code> — adds at position <code>count</code>, then count++.
                Return false if inventory is full.</li>
            <li><code>remove(String name)</code> — find first match by name, shift all
                later items left to close the gap. Set last used slot to null.</li>
            <li><code>contains(String name)</code> — returns true if any item matches</li>
            <li><code>getTotalValue()</code> — sum of all item goldValues</li>
            <li><code>display()</code> — numbered list: "1. Sword [Epic] — Wt:12 Val:250g"</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Why do you need both <code>items.length</code> (capacity) and
            <code>count</code> (how many are stored)? Why not use
            <code>items.length</code> for both?</li>
            <li>Your remove() shifts elements left. If you remove the first item
            from a full 20-slot inventory, how many shifts happen? What if you
            remove the last item?</li>
            <li>What happens if you add 21 items to a 20-slot inventory? Is the
            21st item silently lost, or does your code tell you something?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Acceptance — your FixedInventory must:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Reject add() when full (return false)</li>
            <li>Handle remove() on empty inventory gracefully</li>
            <li>Shift elements correctly — no gaps after remove</li>
            <li>Pass all acceptance tests in the Student RPG Guide</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-06/inventory-builder.html">Inventory Builder (Student RPG Guide)</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-06/array-algorithms.html">Array Algorithms</a> — shift, search, sum</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-06/arrays-of-objects.html">Arrays of Objects</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
